{"data":{"body":"**[P2] Represent an in-flight flush that covers zero exports**\n\nFor the first no-record invocation, an active flush has coverage `0`, which is indistinguishable from the sentinel. A spurious wake or another schedule therefore queues a second flush; the drain returns after the first, and the second exporter call runs afterward. Use `None` or a separate in-flight flag so zero is valid coverage, and test a gated no-record flush with an intermediate notification.","comment_node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPsIIsM7wUrFD","finding_digest":"79cb16e7e6067a6f880e41ab03eeadf8c880f520e61e3aa289e4615a8d6930db","finding_id":"arf_v1_phfrnz7gaz5g7caoigvqh3vn7d","finding_key":"insight/_export_scheduler.py::drain::zero-coverage-flush-inflight-ambiguity","identity_key":"insight/_export_scheduler.py::drain::zero-coverage-flush-inflight-ambiguity","line":175,"observation_digest":"0011e427442a2fcdb30f4f29a1bd841f9d9755ac72543e7b4f6f2ae3cfc4937c","observation_id":"aro_v1_aai6ij2efix43mypj4u2dpmed6","path":"packages/aws-durable-execution-sdk-python-insight/src/aws_durable_execution_sdk_python_insight/_export_scheduler.py","prior_finding_id":"","published_at":"2026-09-17T00:20:38Z","review_id":"arr_v1_33ayiya5fwsl4v4tcidzfuh3ei","reviewed_base_sha":"cf4d27f59c2bf14f87c3ef75f58fc0881b2e2c34","reviewed_head_sha":"fb8af739a92f7fd8070d928029150fe4e5c9cc61","reviewer":"codex","start_line":175,"suggestion_id":""},"pull_request":{"number":734},"record_id":"art_v1_l6qxcpdczeetuwycve4a5cyxga","record_type":"finding_observed","recorded_at":"2026-09-17T00:20:38Z","repository":{"full_name":"aws/aws-durable-execution-sdk-python","id":1052903600},"schema_version":1}
